From: Elizabeth Figura <zfigura@codeweavers.com>
Subject: [Backport Wine 11.0] vkd3d-shader/hlsl: Allow "static" on functions.

Upstream: https://codeberg.org/vkd3d/vkd3d/commit/4746e55a8b3be83bcf3d4b5df89bdabe0e2f4b2d
Wine-Bug: https://bugs.winehq.org/show_bug.cgi?id=59189
Base: Wine 11.0, db11d0fe6a169c457e23d007e20404643d067aa8

Source changes from upstream vkd3d 1.19, with paths adjusted for Wine's
embedded copy. Preserve static declaration checks and entry-point filtering.
This fixes 3DMark06's E5001 "Unexpected modifier used on a function" while
compiling the static skinning helpers in surface/skinned-cubelit-metal.txt.
The same compiler is used by D3DX9 and d3dcompiler; no Vulkan renderer is needed.

Regression: tools/buildWine/probes/hlsl-static-functions.c. Compare the native
D3DX9 compiler, regular Wine modules, and the separate C:/webgl PE modules.
Also launch a 3DMark06 graphics scene with Wine's built-in d3dx9_28.dll.

